{"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"sections":[],"relationshipsSections":[{"kind":"relationships","identifiers":["doc:\/\/Destinations\/documentation\/Destinations\/Destination","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"seeAlsoSections":[{"anchor":"Sending-batches","identifiers":["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDropReport"],"title":"Sending batches","generated":true}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Transport"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"HTTPTransport","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations13HTTPTransportP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransport"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Encoding"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"BatchEncoder","preciseIdentifier":"s:16HTTPDestinations12BatchEncoderP","identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The wire shape, for a server that ingests these batches:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The requests the encoder splits each batch into ("},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder\/requests(for:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"), in the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"order the delivery hands batches over, each request sent only once the previous one is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivered or dropped."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The method is ","type":"text"},{"code":"POST","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and the URL is the configured endpoint.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The header fields are the configured ones, then the trace context of the request’s first","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record, then ","type":"text"},{"code":"Content-Type","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", each replacing fields of the same name before it:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The instrument injects the first (oldest) record’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/context"},{"type":"text","text":", so a server"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"extracting it joins the request, and the events, to the trace the app was in. Its field"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"names are the instrument’s: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"traceparent"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"tracestate"},{"type":"text","text":" for a W3C Trace Context tracer."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A record tracked outside any span, or an instrument that injects nothing (the default"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"NoOpInstrument"},{"type":"text","text":" when none is bootstrapped), adds no fields."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Only the first record’s context travels in the header fields, though a request may hold"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"records tracked in other traces. A server that needs each record’s context reads it from"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the body, where a "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/BatchEncoder"},{"type":"text","text":" writes it."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Content-Type"},{"type":"text","text":" is always the encoder’s "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/contentType","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", whatever a configured"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"field or the instrument wrote."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The body is exactly the encoder’s ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/EncodedBatch\/body","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" for the request’s records, oldest","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"first. The format is the encoder’s; events need no ","type":"text"},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conformance.","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A response with a 2xx status means the batch arrived."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A request the transport can never send (","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPTransportError\/invalidRequest(reason:)","type":"reference","isActive":true},{"text":": a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"malformed or unsupported URL, or an ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"http"},{"text":" URL App Transport Security refuses) isn’t sent","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No response, a 5xx status, 408 Request Timeout or 429 Too Many Requests means it didn’t"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"arrive yet: the same request is sent again after the backoff’s next wait, for as long as it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"takes. A "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Retry-After"},{"type":"text","text":" field is not read; the backoff alone sets the wait."}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Any other status means the endpoint won’t take the request, and it isn’t sent again. The"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"batch’s later requests are still sent."}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A record can arrive twice: a request the server took whose response was lost is sent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"again, and a record a store redelivers after the app was stopped mid-send"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"("},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/isRedelivered"},{"type":"text","text":") may have arrived before. Its "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"EventRecord\/id"},{"type":"text","text":" is the one it was"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"first sent with, so an encoder that writes each record’s identifier lets the server keep one"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"copy."}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A batch of several requests is acknowledged only once every request is delivered or dropped.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"A delivery cancelled, or an app stopped, after some of its requests arrived hands the whole","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"batch over again, so those requests are sent again too: a server that keeps one copy per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"record identifier absorbs them. The records the encoder leaves out are then reported again.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns once the batch is delivered, dropped, or the delivery is cancelled, so","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"a tracker’s store keeps the records of a batch until it arrives, and a batch still being","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"retried when the app ends is delivered again on the next launch. A request the endpoint","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"rejects or that can’t be sent, a batch the encoder can’t encode, and a record the encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"leaves out of its requests are dropped: logged at error level and reported on","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/dropReports","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":". Each failed attempt that will be retried is logged at notice level.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"Cancelling the delivery cancels the send in flight or the wait before the next one, and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations\/HTTPDestination\/receive(_:)","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" returns without logging or reporting it, or sending the batch’s later","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"requests. A request whose wait before the next attempt throws something other than","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"CancellationError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" (a custom clock’s failure) is given up on, logged at error level but not","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"reported, and the batch’s next request is sent.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"While a batch is retried, the delivery’s later batches wait in this destination’s buffer,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"which drops its oldest batch when full and reports it on the delivery’s "},{"code":"bufferDropReports","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"With a store, a dropped batch’s records aren’t lost: once this destination has caught up, the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"delivery reads them back from the store and hands them to it again, in the same run, so they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are sent once the endpoint answers."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Without a store, the records of a dropped batch are lost."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"code":["let collector = HTTPDestination(","    endpoint: collectorURL,","    headerFields: [.authorization: \"Bearer \\(token)\"],","    encoder: PlansEncoder())","let delivery = tracker.records.batch().deliver(to: collector)"],"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing"}]}],"abstract":[{"text":"A destination that sends each batch it receives to an HTTP endpoint, as the requests its encoder","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"splits it into, and sends each again until it arrives.","type":"text"}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HTTPDestinations\/documentation\/HTTPDestinations"]]},"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"HTTPDestinations"}],"title":"HTTPDestination","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HTTPDestination"}],"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HTTPDestination","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:16HTTPDestinations15HTTPDestinationV","symbolKind":"struct","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Traffluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/HTTPDestinations\/